      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect. The answer is clear from the wiki:\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], **the Hub never holds the Anthropic API key in its own process environment.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of the spawned child process** (the Ingest or Query agent), immediately before that process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process were compromised or misbehaved, it could not leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API. The same scoping model applies to both the Ingest and Query agent processes.",
